# Standard library — one tree

File: std/README.oot
All product libraries live here, next to the compiler.
This map is first principles, systems order, and power law.
It is not a copy of another language's folder names.

## 1. Laws

  1. One tree.
  2. A library is code that other programs import. A prove file is not a library.
  3. Proof is emit-c + gcc + run. A folder on disk is not a cert.
  4. Effects need a cap.
  5. Power law: a few modules carry most programs. Work those first.
  6. Systems order: compiler floor, then these trunk modules, then the long tail.

## 2. Power law (priority)

  Trunk (most imports, most proves, do these first)
    result.oo  option.oo  str.oo  byte.oo
    core/  collections/  math/  text/
    encoding/  io/  fs/  net/  os/

  Support (needed when the trunk is honest)
    sync/  actor/  hash/  crypto/  sec/
    markup/  archive/  time/  diag/  test/  simd/

  Tail (field folders at this root: aero, bio, quantum, robot, …)
    Do not certify these until the trunk is done.
    Do not invent a parent folder for them.

  Not libraries
    prove/     named canaries only
    leftover   not a library (no oodac binary, no runtime copy)

## 3. Use

  Import `std/option.oo` and `std/core/list.oo` as before.
  Named product proves live in `ooda/fixtures/prove_prod_*.oo`.

## 4. Residual

  Compiler: generic `Result[T,E]`, richer sums, deeper lists.
  Library: hard-crypto, decompress, full markup, destubs.
  Tail folders wait.
